## 4. Sistema de Diseño (CSS Design System)

### 4.1 Tipografías

```
Google Fonts importados:
- Poppins (400, 500, 600, 700) → Títulos y encabezados
- Open Sans (400, 500, 600) → Texto body y botones
```

### 4.2 Variables CSS (Design Tokens)

#### Colores Principales
```css
--color-primary: #1e40af        /* Azul corporativo */
--color-primary-dark: #1e3a8a   /* Azul oscuro */
--color-secondary: #06d6a0      /* Verde/turquesa accent */
--color-white: #ffffff
--color-dark: #111827
```

#### Escala de Grises
```css
--color-gray-50:  #f9fafb
--color-gray-100: #f3f4f6
--color-gray-200: #e5e7eb
--color-gray-300: #d1d5db
--color-gray-400: #9ca3af
--color-gray-500: #6b7280
--color-gray-800: #1f2937
--color-border:   #e5e7eb
```

#### Glassmorphism
```css
--glass-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7)
--glass-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5)
```

#### Sombras
```css
--shadow-sm:    0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.05)
--shadow:       0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1), 0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)
--shadow-lg:    0 10px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.1), 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.05)
--shadow-glass: 0 8px 32px rgba(31,38,135,0.1)
```

#### Badges de Plataformas
```css
--badge-wa: #25D366                    /* WhatsApp verde */
--badge-ig: linear-gradient(45deg, #f09433, #e6683c, #dc2743, #cc2366, #bc1888)  /* Instagram gradient */
--badge-fb: #1877F2                    /* Facebook azul */
--badge-tg: #229ED9                    /* Telegram azul */
```

### 4.3 Dark Mode

Se implementa mediante el atributo `[data-theme="dark"]` que sobrescribe las variables CSS:

```css
[data-theme="dark"] {
    --color-white: #111827
    --color-gray-50: #030712
    --color-gray-100: #1f2937
    --color-gray-200: #374151
    --color-gray-300: #4b5563
    --color-gray-400: #6b7280
    --color-gray-500: #9ca3af
    --color-gray-800: #f3f4f6
    --color-dark: #f9fafb
    --color-border: #374151
    --glass-bg: rgba(17,24,39,0.7)
    --glass-border: rgba(55,65,81,0.5)
}
```

Componentes con estilos dark específicos:
- `.login-card` → fondo `#111827f2`, sombra más oscura
- `.login-card-header h1/p` → colores invertidos
- `.input-group label` + `.input-with-icon input` → colores adaptados
- `.robot-speech-bubble` → fondo `#1f2937f2`
- `.login-credentials-hint`, `.login-footer`, `.login-error` → ajustados

